   Class-map: VOICE (match-all)
     100 packets, 12000 bytes
     5 minute offered rate 0000 bps, drop rate 0000 bps
     Match: dscp ef (46)
     Queueing
       Strict Priority$$::text, $$[{"id": "A", "text": "Best-effort queueing", "is_correct": false}, {"id": "B", "text": "Class-Based Weighted Fair Queuing", "is_correct": false}, {"id": "C", "text": "Low Latency Queueing (strict priority)", "is_correct": true}, {"id": "D", "text": "Traffic shaping", "is_correct": false}]$$::jsonb, $$The output shows 'Strict Priority' for the VOICE class, indicating LLQ.$$::text, $${"https://learningcontent.cisco.com/documents/marketing/exam-topics/200-301-CCNA-v1.1.pdf"}$$::text[], $$4.0 IP Services$$::text, 10.0, 'cece6320ea4fc44a', true) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
-- +goose StatementEnd

