Pro Inside global      Inside local       Outside local      Outside global
--- 203.0.113.10       192.168.1.10       ---                ---$$::text, $$[{"id": "A", "text": "Dynamic NAT with overload", "is_correct": false}, {"id": "B", "text": "Static one-to-one NAT", "is_correct": true}, {"id": "C", "text": "PAT many-to-one", "is_correct": false}, {"id": "D", "text": "Destination NAT", "is_correct": false}]$$::jsonb, $$A single inside global address is mapped to a single inside local address, indicating static NAT.$$::text, $${"https://learningcontent.cisco.com/documents/marketing/exam-topics/200-301-CCNA-v1.1.pdf"}$$::text[], $$4.0 IP Services$$::text, 10.0, 'a1833e1924c6f6eb', true) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
